 "10": {
  "name": "Glendo State Park",
  "description": "Glendo State Park is a 22,000 acre park in Platte County\u202fWyoming, and exists on and around Glendo Reservoir.\u202fWith 10,000 acres of land and 12,000 acres of water, our\u202fpark has a wide variety of recreation options, which are open and accessible year-round!\u202fWe\u202fhave 45 miles of multi-use, non-motorized trails, which make for excellent hiking and biking for expert and novice trail users alike. Six boat ramps provide seasonal water access for all manner of boaters. If you're looking to fish, Glendo Reservoir is home to one of the best walleye fisheries in the state, along with healthy populations of",
